nch-ab/results/opencode-src/bin/006d673ed2e795ce41f30fc240189a54ff12c231/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": true, "members_read_calls": 1, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: read]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\nApplying fixes now.\n[tool: bash]\nLine 3 of `catalog/members.py`, quoted exactly:\n\n> `# The lending policy allows each member to hold five books at once.`\n\nI fixed the code in `catalog/` without touching the tests, and `python3 -m unittest` now passes all 16 tests. The first run showed 15 tests because `tests/test_search.py` couldn't be imported.\n\nFixes:\n- **`catalog/members.py:4`**: `MAX_BORROWED` was `3`, but the comment on line 3 and the tests both say five books. Changed it to `5`.\n- **`catalog/search.py:3`**: it imported `normalize` from a module that doesn't exist (`catalog.nonexistent`). It now imports from `catalog.text`.\n- **`catalog/books.py:22`**: `parse_book` kept the year as a string, which broke `age()`. It now converts the year with `int(year)`.\n- **`catalog/fees.py:14`**: the fee was days *plus* the daily rate. It's now days *times* the rate (`days_late * DAILY_FEE`).\n- **`catalog/inventory.py:24`**: `recent(n)` returned one event too many. It now returns `self._history[-n:]`, and an empty list when `n` is 0 or less, because `[-0:]` would otherwise return the whole history.\n- **`catalog/factory.py`**: added the missing `Emma` book (Austen, 1815, 1 copy) to `sample_books()`, which its docstring already lists.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": ["param:temperature"], "params_stripped_requests": 1, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 34346, "requests_cache_write": 46908, "requests_cost_usd": 0.2667852, "requests_count": 5, "requests_inpu